IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fcr-dates`
IMPORT `fcr-rules`

-- Federal Court Rules 2011 (Cth) -- the questions of the individual party to a claim in the Federal Court of Australia:
-- usually the applicant who brings it (an injured person, an employee, a person discriminated against, a claimant for
-- compensation), and, where a step falls on the person answering it, that person as respondent or appeal respondent.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Federal Court Rules 2011", Compilation No. 11
-- (11 June 2026), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts only. What the Court decides (leave, whether it is satisfied, whether a failure was
-- unreasonable) is asked as a fact: "if the Court ...". A yes about the Court means the Court can do it, not that it
-- will. The Court can extend or shorten any time (r 1.39) and make orders inconsistent with the Rules (r 1.35).
-- Day counting follows r 1.61; business days leave out Saturdays, Sundays and 1 January, 26 January, 25 April,
-- 25 and 26 December only: other public holidays and Registry closures are not known here.

§ `Federal Court Rules 2011 -- my questions as a party to a claim`

§§ `Counting time and filing (rr 1.61, 2.25)`

@export What is the last day of a period of days the Federal Court Rules 2011 or a Federal Court order give me to do something (r 1.61)? The day of the event is not counted; for periods of 5 days or less, weekends and public holidays are not counted; no day from 24 December to 14 January is counted; a filing deadline on a non-business day moves to the next business day.
GIVEN `the day the period runs from` IS A DATE @desc From what day does the period run (the day of the event, e.g. the day you were served), ISO date e.g. 2026-03-15?
      `how many days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the rule or order give you (e.g. 28)?
      `it is a filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the step one that can only be done on a business day, such as filing a document in the Registry?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day of my period?` `the day the period runs from` `how many days` `it is a filing` MEANS
    `r 1.61 -- the last day of n days after` `the day the period runs from` `how many days` `it is a filing`

@export On what day is a document I email or fax to the Federal Court Registry taken to be filed (r 2.25(3) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? That day if the whole document arrives by 4.30 pm on a business day; otherwise the next business day.
GIVEN `the day it arrived` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the whole document reach the Registry (ISO date)?
      `it arrived by 4.30 pm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the whole document arrive by 4.30 pm (Registry local time) that day?
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day is my document filed?` `the day it arrived` `it arrived by 4.30 pm` MEANS
    `r 2.25(3) -- the day it is taken to be filed` `the day it arrived` `it arrived by 4.30 pm`

@export On what day am I taken to have been served with a document in my Federal Court case (r 10.32 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? By post, the seventh business day after posting; by fax or email, the next business day after sending; handed to me personally, that day.
GIVEN `the day it was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the document posted, faxed, emailed or handed to you (ISO date)?
      `how it was sent` IS A `Means of service` @desc How was it served: "personal service", "pre-paid post", "fax" or "electronic communication" (email)?
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day am I served?` `the day it was sent` `how it was sent` MEANS
    `r 10.32 -- the day I am taken to be served` `the day it was sent` `how it was sent`

§§ `Starting my claim (rr 8.02, 8.03, 8.05, 8.06)`

@export Must I file a genuine steps statement with my originating application in the Federal Court (r 8.02 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes if Part 2 of the Civil Dispute Resolution Act 2011 applies to the proceeding.
GIVEN `the Civil Dispute Resolution Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Part 2 of the Civil Dispute Resolution Act 2011 apply to your proceeding (it applies to most civil claims; some kinds, such as many Fair Work and migration matters, are excluded by that Act)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I file a genuine steps statement?` `the Civil Dispute Resolution Act applies` MEANS
    `r 8.02 -- I must file a genuine steps statement` `the Civil Dispute Resolution Act applies`

@export What document must go with my originating application in the Federal Court (r 8.05 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? A claim for damages needs a statement of claim; other claims a statement of claim or an affidavit; a practice note may require or permit an alternative document instead.
GIVEN `I claim damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the relief you claim include damages (money compensation for loss or injury)?
      `the practice note` IS A `Practice note position` @desc Does a Chief Justice's practice note for your kind of case provide for an alternative accompanying document? One of: "no practice note provides for an alternative document", "a practice note requires an alternative accompanying document", "a practice note permits an alternative accompanying document".
GIVETH AN `Accompanying document`
`What must go with my originating application?` `I claim damages` `the practice note` MEANS
    `r 8.05 -- what must accompany the originating application` `I claim damages` `the practice note`

@export If I claim exemplary damages, must my originating application say so (r 8.03(2) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes: the claim for exemplary damages must be stated. A claim for costs need not be included.
GIVEN `I claim exemplary damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming exemplary (punitive) damages?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I state my exemplary damages claim?` `I claim exemplary damages` MEANS
    `r 8.03(2) -- I must state the exemplary damages claim` `I claim exemplary damages`

@export By when must I personally serve my originating application on each respondent (r 8.06 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? As soon as practicable, and at least 5 days (business days, not counting 24 December to 14 January) before the first directions hearing or the hearing, whichever is earlier.
GIVEN `the first directions hearing` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the first directions hearing (the return date endorsed on the application), ISO date?
      `the hearing` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the hearing, if one is fixed (ISO date)? If none is fixed, give the same date as the first directions hearing.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I serve my originating application?` `the first directions hearing` `the hearing` MEANS
    `r 8.06 -- the last day to serve the originating application` `the first directions hearing` `the hearing`

§§ `The defence, the reply and default (rr 16.32, 16.33, 5.22, 5.23)`

@export By when must the respondent file a defence to my statement of claim, or if I am the respondent, by when must I file mine (r 16.32 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 28 days after service of the statement of claim.
GIVEN `the day the statement of claim was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the statement of claim served on the respondent (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the defence be filed?` `the day the statement of claim was served` MEANS
    `r 16.32 -- the last day to file a defence` `the day the statement of claim was served`

@export By when must I file a reply to the respondent's defence (r 16.33 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 14 days after being served with the defence, if you want to plead a matter that must be pleaded in reply.
GIVEN `the day the defence was served on me` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you served with the defence (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I file my reply?` `the day the defence was served on me` MEANS
    `r 16.33 -- the last day to file a reply` `the day the defence was served on me`

@export Is the respondent to my claim in default (r 5.22 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? A party is in default if it fails to do an act in the time the Rules require (here, file a defence within 28 days after service of the statement of claim), fails to comply with an order, fails to attend a hearing, or fails to defend with due diligence.
GIVEN `the day the statement of claim was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your statement of claim served on the respondent (ISO date)?
      `a defence has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent filed a defence?
      `the day the defence was filed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day was it filed (ISO date)? If not, give any date.
      `today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date (ISO date)?
      `it failed to comply with an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent failed to comply with an order of the Court?
      `it failed to attend a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent failed to attend a hearing in the proceeding?
      `it failed to defend with due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent failed to defend the proceeding with due diligence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the respondent in default?` `the day the statement of claim was served` `a defence has been filed` `the day the defence was filed` `today` `it failed to comply with an order` `it failed to attend a hearing` `it failed to defend with due diligence` MEANS
    `r 5.22 -- the respondent is in default` `the day the statement of claim was served` `a defence has been filed` `the day the defence was filed` `today` `it failed to comply with an order` `it failed to attend a hearing` `it failed to defend with due diligence`

@export If the respondent is in default, what judgment can I ask the Federal Court for (r 5.23(2) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? For a debt or liquidated damages, judgment for that sum with interest and costs; on a statement of claim, the relief the Court is satisfied I am entitled to; otherwise judgment for damages to be assessed or any other order.
GIVEN `the respondent is in default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the respondent in default (for example, no defence filed in time)?
      `my claim is for a debt or a fixed sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for a debt or liquidated damages (a fixed or calculable sum, not damages a court must assess, such as for personal injury)?
      `my claim has a statement of claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your proceeding started with a statement of claim (or an alternative accompanying document), or has the Court ordered that it continue on pleadings?
GIVETH A `Default order`
`What judgment can I get on default?` `the respondent is in default` `my claim is for a debt or a fixed sum` `my claim has a statement of claim` MEANS
    `r 5.23(2) -- the judgment I can apply for` `the respondent is in default` `my claim is for a debt or a fixed sum` `my claim has a statement of claim`

§§ `Medical examinations (r 23.21) -- only where my physical or mental condition is in question`

@export Must I attend a medical examination the other side wants in my Federal Court claim (r 23.21 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? A notice from the other party only requests it and the rule states no duty to attend on a notice alone; if the Court orders it, you must attend and do what the expert reasonably asks.
GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your physical or mental condition relevant to a matter in question in the case (e.g. you claim for an injury)?
      `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party, or a person for whose benefit a party claims relief?
      `the basis` IS AN `Examination basis` @desc Why are you asked to attend: "a notice from another party requesting it", "an order of the Court", or "neither"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I attend the medical examination?` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` MEANS
    `r 23.21 -- I must submit to the examination` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis`

@export Can I bring a doctor or other health professional of my own choice to the medical examination (r 23.21(3) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes, if they are registered or licensed under State or Territory law in a health or allied health profession.
GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your physical or mental condition relevant to a matter in question in the case?
      `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party, or a person for whose benefit a party claims relief?
      `the basis` IS AN `Examination basis` @desc Why is the examination happening: "a notice from another party requesting it", "an order of the Court", or "neither"?
      `my expert is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you want to bring registered or licensed under State or Territory law in a health or allied health profession (e.g. doctor, dentist, psychologist, physiotherapist, occupational therapist, optometrist)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I bring my own expert to the examination?` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` `my expert is registered` MEANS
    `r 23.21(3) -- I may bring my own medical expert` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` `my expert is registered`

@export Must the party who asked for my medical examination pay my travel and other expenses, including my own expert's attendance (r 23.21(4) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes for an examination requested by notice, once you ask for a reasonable sum.
GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your physical or mental condition relevant to a matter in question in the case?
      `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party, or a person for whose benefit a party claims relief?
      `the basis` IS AN `Examination basis` @desc Why is the examination happening: "a notice from another party requesting it", "an order of the Court", or "neither"?
      `I asked for my expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked that party to pay your expenses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my examination expenses be paid?` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` `I asked for my expenses` MEANS
    `r 23.21(4) -- the other party must pay my expenses` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` `I asked for my expenses`

@export Must I be given a copy of the medical report from the examination (r 23.21(5) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes for an examination requested by notice: the party who served the notice must get the report and serve a copy on you as soon as reasonably practicable.
GIVEN `my condition is in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your physical or mental condition relevant to a matter in question in the case?
      `I am a party or claimed for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party, or a person for whose benefit a party claims relief?
      `the basis` IS AN `Examination basis` @desc Why was the examination held: "a notice from another party requesting it", "an order of the Court", or "neither"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I get a copy of the medical report?` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis` MEANS
    `r 23.21(5) -- I must be served with the report` `my condition is in question` `I am a party or claimed for` `the basis`

§§ `Offers to settle (Part 25)`

@export Is the time my offer to settle (offer to compromise) stays open long enough under the Federal Court Rules 2011 (rr 25.05(3), 25.08(1))? It must be at least 14 days after the offer is made, not counting the day of the offer or 24 December to 14 January.
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offer made (served), ISO date?
      `the closing day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for acceptance stated in the offer (ISO date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my offer open long enough?` `the day the offer was made` `the closing day` MEANS
    `r 25.08(1) -- the time for acceptance is long enough` `the day the offer was made` `the closing day`

@export Can I still accept the other side's offer to settle on this day (r 25.08 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within the time the offer states (never less than 14 days), or if it states none, at any time before judgment; not once it has been withdrawn.
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offer made (ISO date)?
      `it states a closing day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer state a time by which it must be accepted?
      `the closing day` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day for acceptance it states (ISO date); otherwise any date.
      `it has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the offer been withdrawn (validly, under r 25.07)?
      `judgment has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has judgment been given in the proceeding?
      `the day I accept` IS A DATE @desc On what day will you serve your notice of acceptance (ISO date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still accept the offer?` `the day the offer was made` `it states a closing day` `the closing day` `it has been withdrawn` `judgment has been given` `the day I accept` MEANS
    `r 25.08 -- I can accept the offer` `the day the offer was made` `it states a closing day` `the closing day` `it has been withdrawn` `judgment has been given` `the day I accept`

@export Can I withdraw my own offer to settle (r 25.07 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 14 days after making it, only with the Court's leave or by replacing it with an offer more favourable to the other side. After 14 days the rule does not answer.
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the offer (ISO date)?
      `the day I withdraw` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to withdraw it (ISO date)?
      `the Court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, on your application, given leave to withdraw it?
      `I replace it with a better offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you replacing it with an offer on terms more favourable to the other side?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I withdraw my offer?` `the day the offer was made` `the day I withdraw` `the Court gives leave` `I replace it with a better offer` MEANS
    `r 25.07 -- I can withdraw my offer` `the day the offer was made` `the day I withdraw` `the Court gives leave` `I replace it with a better offer`

@export I accepted an offer of money. By when must it be paid to me (r 25.04 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 28 days after acceptance (not counting 24 December to 14 January), unless the offer gives another time.
GIVEN `the day I accepted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you serve your notice of acceptance (ISO date)?
      `the offer gives its own payment time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer itself say when the money will be paid?
      `the payment day in the offer` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day for payment it gives (ISO date); otherwise any date.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the accepted offer be paid?` `the day I accepted` `the offer gives its own payment time` `the payment day in the offer` MEANS
    `r 25.04 -- the last day for payment` `the day I accepted` `the offer gives its own payment time` `the payment day in the offer`

@export I accepted an offer of money but was not paid on time. Can I withdraw my acceptance (r 25.09 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Only if the money was not paid within 28 days after acceptance (or the offer's own time) and the Court gives leave.
GIVEN `the day I accepted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you serve your notice of acceptance (ISO date)?
      `the offer gives its own payment time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the offer itself say when the money will be paid?
      `the payment day in the offer` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day for payment it gives (ISO date); otherwise any date.
      `I have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the money been paid to you?
      `the day I was paid` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day (ISO date)? Otherwise any date.
      `today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date (ISO date)?
      `the Court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, on your application, given leave to withdraw the acceptance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I withdraw my acceptance?` `the day I accepted` `the offer gives its own payment time` `the payment day in the offer` `I have been paid` `the day I was paid` `today` `the Court gives leave` MEANS
    `r 25.09 -- I can withdraw my acceptance` `the day I accepted` `the offer gives its own payment time` `the payment day in the offer` `I have been paid` `the day I was paid` `today` `the Court gives leave`

@export I accepted an offer that did not include my costs. Up to what day can I have my costs taxed against the other side (r 25.12 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Party and party costs up to and including 14 days after the offer was made.
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offer made (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`Up to when are my costs covered after accepting?` `the day the offer was made` MEANS
    `r 25.12 -- my costs run up to` `the day the offer was made`

@export From when do the costs consequences of an unaccepted offer to settle start (rr 25.13, 25.14 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? 11.00 am on the second business day after the offer was served; this gives that day.
GIVEN `the day the offer was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offer served (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day is the offer costs cut-off?` `the day the offer was served` MEANS
    `r 25.14 -- the day of the 11 am cut-off` `the day the offer was served`

@export What costs follow if an offer to settle my Federal Court claim was not accepted (r 25.14 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? If I refused the respondent's offer and did worse at judgment, I lose my costs after the cut-off and pay the respondent's on an indemnity basis; if my own offer was refused and I did better, the respondent pays my costs, on an indemnity basis after the cut-off. The Court may order otherwise.
GIVEN `who made it` IS A `Who made the offer` @desc Who made the offer: "the respondent made the offer to me" or "I made the offer to the respondent"?
      `it was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offer accepted?
      `the outcome` IS A `How my claim ended` @desc How did your claim end compared with the offer: "I got judgment less favourable to me than the offer", "I got judgment as favourable to me as the offer", "I got judgment more favourable to me than the offer", or "my proceeding was dismissed"?
      `the Court finds I unreasonably refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if the respondent made the offer and your claim was dismissed: does the Court find that you unreasonably failed to accept it?
GIVETH AN `Offer costs consequence`
`What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `who made it` `it was accepted` `the outcome` `the Court finds I unreasonably refused` MEANS
    `r 25.14 -- the costs consequence of the offer` `who made it` `it was accepted` `the outcome` `the Court finds I unreasonably refused`

§§ `Ending my claim early (rr 26.01, 26.12, 26.15, 39.03)`

@export The respondent applies for summary judgment against me. By when must I have been served with the application and its affidavit (r 26.01(3) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? At least 14 days before the hearing of the application, not counting 24 December to 14 January.
GIVEN `the hearing of the application` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the summary judgment application to be heard (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I be served with a summary judgment application?` `the hearing of the application` MEANS
    `r 26.01(3) -- the last day to serve a summary judgment application` `the hearing of the application`

@export Can I discontinue (drop) my Federal Court claim, and do I need the other side's consent or the Court's leave (r 26.12 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Without either before the first directions hearing or hearing (or before pleadings close); with consent before judgment is entered; with leave at any time. A representative party or litigation representative always needs leave.
GIVEN `the first directions hearing` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or was) the first directions hearing (ISO date)?
      `the hearing` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or was) the hearing (ISO date)? If none is fixed, give the first directions hearing date.
      `the day I discontinue` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you file the notice of discontinuance (ISO date)?
      `my claim is on pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your proceeding continuing on pleadings (statement of claim, defence, reply)?
      `the pleadings have closed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the pleadings closed?
      `judgment has been entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has judgment been entered in the proceeding?
      `I am a representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you acting as a litigation representative for someone (e.g. a child) or as a representative party for a group?
GIVETH A `Way to discontinue`
`How can I discontinue my claim?` `the first directions hearing` `the hearing` `the day I discontinue` `my claim is on pleadings` `the pleadings have closed` `judgment has been entered` `I am a representative` MEANS
    `r 26.12 -- how I can discontinue` `the first directions hearing` `the hearing` `the day I discontinue` `my claim is on pleadings` `the pleadings have closed` `judgment has been entered` `I am a representative`

@export If I discontinue my Federal Court claim, must I pay the other side's costs of it (r 26.12(7) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes, unless the terms of a consent or a Court order say otherwise.
GIVEN `a consent or order says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms of the other side's consent, or an order of the Court, provide otherwise about costs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I pay costs if I discontinue?` `a consent or order says otherwise` MEANS
    `r 26.12(7) -- I must pay the other side's costs of what I discontinue` `a consent or order says otherwise`

@export If I sue again after discontinuing, or after my claim was dismissed with costs against me, can my new case be held up until I pay those costs (rr 26.14, 26.15, 39.03(2) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes, on the other side's application, if the costs are unpaid and the new case is on the same or substantially the same cause of action.
GIVEN `how it ended` IS A `How my earlier proceeding ended` @desc How did your earlier proceeding end: "I discontinued it and became liable for the other party's costs", "it was dismissed and I was ordered to pay the other party's costs", or "some other way"?
      `I have paid those costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid those costs?
      `same cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new case on the same, or substantially the same, cause of action (or relief) against the same party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my new case be stayed until I pay costs?` `how it ended` `I have paid those costs` `same cause of action` MEANS
    `rr 26.15, 39.03(2) -- my new proceeding can be stayed until I pay` `how it ended` `I have paid those costs` `same cause of action`

§§ `Damages calculated by a Registrar (rr 30.41-30.43)`

@export Can my damages be calculated by a Registrar instead of at a trial (r 30.41 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? If the respondent admits liability but not the amount, or the Court has found liability for damages, and the Court is satisfied the amount is substantially a matter of calculation.
GIVEN `liability admitted but not the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent admitted liability on your claim but denied the amount of damages claimed?
      `the Court found liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court found that a party is liable to pay you damages?
      `the Court is satisfied it is calculation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the amount of damages is substantially a matter of calculation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can a Registrar calculate my damages?` `liability admitted but not the amount` `the Court found liability` `the Court is satisfied it is calculation` MEANS
    `r 30.41 -- my damages can be calculated by a Registrar` `liability admitted but not the amount` `the Court found liability` `the Court is satisfied it is calculation`

@export By when must I object to the Registrar's certificate of my damages (r 30.42 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 7 days after receiving it: give the Registrar notice and serve each other party.
GIVEN `the day I received the certificate` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the Registrar's certificate (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I object to the damages certificate?` `the day I received the certificate` MEANS
    `r 30.42 -- the last day to object to the certificate` `the day I received the certificate`

@export After objecting to the Registrar's damages certificate, by when must I apply for the Court to assess my damages (r 30.43 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 21 days after giving notice of objection.
GIVEN `the day I gave notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the Registrar your notice of objection (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for the Court to assess damages?` `the day I gave notice` MEANS
    `r 30.43 -- the last day to apply for the Court to assess damages` `the day I gave notice`

§§ `Appeals (Parts 35 and 36) -- only after a judgment or order I want to challenge, or an appeal against me`

@export By when must I apply for leave to appeal from a judgment or order in the Federal Court (r 35.13 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 14 days after the judgment or order, or by a later date the Court fixed. The Court can extend time (r 35.14).
GIVEN `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the judgment pronounced or the order made (ISO date)?
      `the Court fixed a date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court fix a date for filing the application for leave?
      `the date fixed` IS A DATE @desc If so, that date (ISO date); otherwise any date.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for leave to appeal?` `the day of the judgment` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed` MEANS
    `r 35.13 -- the last day to apply for leave to appeal` `the day of the judgment` `the Court fixed a date` `the date fixed`

@export By when must I serve my application for leave to appeal (r 35.15 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 2 days of filing it, counting business days only.
GIVEN `the day I filed` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you file the application (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I serve my leave application?` `the day I filed` MEANS
    `r 35.15 -- the last day to serve the leave application` `the day I filed`

@export By when must I file my notice of appeal to the Federal Court (r 36.03 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 28 days after the judgment (or after leave to appeal was granted), or by a later date the court appealed from fixed. The Court can extend time (r 36.05).
GIVEN `the kind of appeal` IS A `Kind of appeal` @desc Is it "an appeal as of right" or "an appeal by leave" (you needed and got leave to appeal)?
      `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the judgment appealed from pronounced or the order made (ISO date)?
      `the day leave was granted` IS A DATE @desc For an appeal by leave, on what day was leave granted (ISO date)? Otherwise any date.
      `a date was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the court appealed from fix a date for filing the notice of appeal?
      `the date fixed` IS A DATE @desc If so, that date (ISO date); otherwise any date.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I file my notice of appeal?` `the kind of appeal` `the day of the judgment` `the day leave was granted` `a date was fixed` `the date fixed` MEANS
    `r 36.03 -- the last day to file a notice of appeal` `the kind of appeal` `the day of the judgment` `the day leave was granted` `a date was fixed` `the date fixed`

@export I appeal from a State or Territory court. By when must I lodge a copy of my notice of appeal with that court (r 36.04(2) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 7 days after filing it.
GIVEN `the day I filed` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you file the notice of appeal (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I lodge a copy with the lower court?` `the day I filed` MEANS
    `r 36.04(2) -- the last day to lodge a copy with the State or Territory court` `the day I filed`

@export Can I amend my notice of appeal without the Court's leave on this day (r 36.10 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes during the 28 days after filing it, by filing a supplementary notice of appeal.
GIVEN `the day I filed` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you file the notice of appeal (ISO date)?
      `the day I amend` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you file the supplementary notice (ISO date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I amend my notice of appeal without leave?` `the day I filed` `the day I amend` MEANS
    `r 36.10 -- I can amend my notice of appeal without leave` `the day I filed` `the day I amend`

-- Situation: only where the other side has appealed and the person is the respondent to the appeal.
@export The other side has appealed. By when must I file my notice of address for service, cross-appeal or notice of contention (rr 36.07, 36.22, 36.24 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Address for service within 14 days, cross-appeal or notice of contention within 21 days, after being served with the notice of appeal.
GIVEN `the step` IS A `Respondent's appeal step` @desc Which step: "a notice of address for service", "a notice of cross-appeal" or "a notice of contention"?
      `the day I was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you served with the notice of appeal (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I take my step in the appeal?` `the step` `the day I was served` MEANS
    `rr 36.07, 36.22, 36.24 -- the last day for my step in the appeal` `the step` `the day I was served`

§§ `Judgments, orders and interest (Part 39)`

@export By when must I do what a Federal Court order requires of me, or pay money into Court (r 39.02 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? In the time the order specifies, or if none, within 14 days after the order is served on me.
GIVEN `the order gives a time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order say by when you must do it?
      `the last day in the order` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day it gives (ISO date); otherwise any date.
      `the day it was served on me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the order served on you (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I comply with the order?` `the order gives a time` `the last day in the order` `the day it was served on me` MEANS
    `r 39.02 -- the last day to comply with the order` `the order gives a time` `the last day in the order` `the day it was served on me`

@export Can the Federal Court set aside or vary a judgment or order in my case (rr 39.04, 39.05 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Before it is entered, yes; within 14 days after entry, on an application filed in that time (which the Court cannot extend); after that, only on a listed ground such as absence, fraud, a slip or consent.
GIVEN `it has been entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judgment or order been entered (authenticated by signature and seal)?
      `the day it was entered` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day (ISO date)? Otherwise any date.
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc On what day would you file your application (ISO date)?
      `the ground` IS A `Ground to set aside after entry` @desc Which ground applies, if any: "it was made in my absence", "it was obtained by fraud", "it is interlocutory", "it is an injunction or appoints a receiver", "it does not reflect the intention of the Court", "the party it favours consents", "there is a clerical mistake in it", "there is an error from an accidental slip or omission", or "none of these"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the judgment be set aside or varied?` `it has been entered` `the day it was entered` `the day I apply` `the ground` MEANS
    `rr 39.04, 39.05 -- the judgment can be set aside or varied` `it has been entered` `the day it was entered` `the day I apply` `the ground`

@export What rate of interest runs on a Federal Court judgment debt owed to me (r 39.06 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? 6 percentage points above the Reserve Bank cash rate last published before the half-year (1 January or 1 July) began, unless the Court sets a lower rate.
GIVEN `the cash rate` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Reserve Bank of Australia cash rate, in percent (e.g. 3.85), last published before 1 January or 1 July starting the half-year in question?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What interest runs on my judgment?` `the cash rate` MEANS
    `r 39.06 -- the interest rate on a judgment debt` `the cash rate`

@export For a day, from which date must I take the Reserve Bank cash rate to work out Federal Court judgment interest (r 39.06 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? The half-year starts 1 January or 1 July; the rate is the one last published before that date.
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For what day do you want the interest rate (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`When does the interest half-year start?` `the day in question` MEANS
    `r 39.06 -- the start of the half-year` `the day in question`

§§ `Costs (Part 40)`

@export Who bears the costs of an interlocutory application or hearing in my case when the Court made no costs order (r 40.04 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? They follow the event if the order favoured a party; otherwise they are costs in the cause of whoever wins the proceeding.
GIVEN `a costs order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court make an order about the costs of the application?
      `the outcome` IS AN `Interlocutory costs outcome` @desc What was the result: "the order on the application was in my favour", "the order on the application was in the other party's favour", or "no order was made in favour of any party"?
GIVETH AN `Interlocutory costs result`
`Who bears the interlocutory costs?` `a costs order was made` `the outcome` MEANS
    `r 40.04 -- who bears the interlocutory costs` `a costs order was made` `the outcome`

@export I won my Federal Court claim. Can the other side ask the Court to reduce the costs it must pay me (r 40.08 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes if I claimed money or damages and was awarded less than $100 000, or if the claim could more suitably have been brought in another court or tribunal (not in Admiralty proceedings).
GIVEN `I claimed money or damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you claim a sum of money or damages?
      `the sum awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc How much were you awarded, in Australian dollars?
      `the Court thinks another court was more suitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court consider the proceeding could more suitably have been brought in another court or tribunal (e.g. a State court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court)?
      `it is an Admiralty proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a proceeding under the Admiralty Act 1988?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my costs be reduced?` `I claimed money or damages` `the sum awarded` `the Court thinks another court was more suitable` `it is an Admiralty proceeding` MEANS
    `r 40.08 -- the costs payable to me can be reduced` `I claimed money or damages` `the sum awarded` `the Court thinks another court was more suitable` `it is an Admiralty proceeding`

@export Can I have the costs I was awarded on an interlocutory application taxed now (r 40.13 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Not until the proceeding is finished, unless the Court orders immediate taxation.
GIVEN `the proceeding is finished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the whole proceeding finished?
      `the Court ordered immediate taxation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court order that those costs be taxed immediately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I tax my interlocutory costs now?` `the proceeding is finished` `the Court ordered immediate taxation` MEANS
    `r 40.13 -- I can tax my interlocutory costs now` `the proceeding is finished` `the Court ordered immediate taxation`

@export By when must I object to the taxing officer's estimate of a costs bill, and pay in the $2 000 security (r 40.21 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 21 days after the notice of estimate issues.
GIVEN `the day the notice of estimate issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice of estimate issued (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I object to the costs estimate?` `the day the notice of estimate issued` MEANS
    `r 40.21 -- the last day to object to the estimate` `the day the notice of estimate issued`

@export How much must I pay into the Litigants' Fund as security if I object to the costs estimate (r 40.21(1)(b) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? $2 000.
GIVEN `I object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you objecting to the taxing officer's estimate?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much security must I pay to object?` `I object` MEANS
    IF `I object`
    THEN `r 40.21(1)(b) -- the security to pay in on objecting`
    ELSE 0

@export By when must I ask for a full taxation after a provisional taxation of a costs bill (r 40.23(4) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 21 days after the taxing officer's written notice.
GIVEN `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the taxing officer's written notice of the provisional taxation given (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I ask for a full taxation?` `the day of the notice` MEANS
    `r 40.23(4) -- the last day to ask for a full taxation` `the day of the notice`

@export I objected to the costs estimate. Must I pay everyone's costs of the taxation (r 40.33 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Yes, unless the bill is taxed at more than 115% of the estimate (if you filed the bill) or less than 85% of it (if you are paying it).
GIVEN `I objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you object to the estimate under r 40.21?
      `I filed the bill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file the bill (you are the party claiming the costs)?
      `the estimate` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the taxing officer's estimate, in Australian dollars?
      `the amount taxed` IS A NUMBER @desc For what amount was the bill taxed, in Australian dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I pay the costs of the taxation?` `I objected` `I filed the bill` `the estimate` `the amount taxed` MEANS
    `r 40.33 -- I must pay the costs of the taxation` `I objected` `I filed the bill` `the estimate` `the amount taxed`

@export I attended the taxation of a costs bill. By when must I file and serve an application for the Court to review it (r 40.34(4) of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 28 days after the certificate of taxation issues.
GIVEN `the day the certificate issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the certificate of taxation issued (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to review the taxation?` `the day the certificate issued` MEANS
    `r 40.34 -- the last day to apply for review of the taxation` `the day the certificate issued`

@export By when must the party who filed a costs bill serve the certificate of taxation on the party paying (r 40.32 of the Federal Court Rules 2011)? Within 14 days after it issues.
GIVEN `the day the certificate issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the certificate of taxation issued (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the certificate of taxation be served?` `the day the certificate issued` MEANS
    `r 40.32 -- the last day to serve the certificate of taxation` `the day the certificate issued`
